From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:47:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: keep the spike's own key in the vault, held while it is
 open

The study's vault-gated key (encri-firefox W6): 32 random bytes in a
document named encriox.key, in the folder the vault allows the browser.
The gate reads it once the vault is open, or makes it there and reads
it back before using it, and holds it in memory alone until the vault
locks or the session ends. A document of the wrong length, two of the
name, or one that does not read back are refused, never written over.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
